USER AGREEMENT (OFFER)
for the application for Windows OS "Bus Fleet 'Blacklist' of Gomel City"

1. GENERAL PROVISIONS
1.1. This User Agreement (hereinafter referred to as the "Agreement" ) is a public offer addressed to an indefinite circle of persons, in accordance with Article 392 of the Civil Code of the Republic of Belarus (hereinafter — "CC RB" ), concluded between the User and the Service Administration, which is a state-owned unitary enterprise "Gomel Bus Park No. 1" (hereinafter — "Company" or "Administration" ).

1.2. For the purposes of this Agreement:

"User" — a capable physical or legal entity who, acting on their own behalf or on behalf of a represented party, accesses the functionality of the Service, including but not limited to using the application for Windows OS, website, API, and other system components;
"Services" — a set of services and products provided by the Company through software accessible via the application for Windows OS and/or web interface;
"Program" — software intended to perform functions related to informing about public transport schedules, tracking buses, notification systems, and other functional modules;
"Data" — any data transmitted, processed, stored, or used within the User's interaction with the Services;
"Personal Data" — information relating to a specific or identifiable individual, subject to processing in accordance with the Law of the Republic of Belarus dated May 7, 2021 No. 85-Z “On Personal Data Protection”;
"Paid Services" — additional features available on a paid basis, including subscriptions, paid notifications, exclusive content, and other products offered by the Company.
1.3. Use of the Services, including installation, launch, viewing, downloading, registration, authorization, use of functionality, or any other interaction with the Program, automatically constitutes unconditional acceptance of the terms of this Agreement as a condition of an adhesion contract pursuant to Article 406 CC RB.

1.4. The Company may amend or supplement this Agreement unilaterally without prior notice to the User unless otherwise provided by applicable legislation. The User must independently verify the current version. The date of the last change is indicated at the end of the document.

1.5. If the User disagrees with the terms of the Agreement, they must cease using the Services.

2. TERMS AND DEFINITIONS
2.1. For the purposes of this Agreement, the following terms are used:

"Authorization" — the process of identifying the User using login, phone number, email, or other credentials established by the Administration.
"Registration" — the procedure for creating a User account associated with providing accurate personal data and verification.
"Account" — the individual profile of the User created within the Service and providing access to its functions.
"Content" — textual, graphic, video, audio, software, and other materials posted by the User or third parties within the use of the Services.
"Intellectual Property" — objects of exclusive rights, including computer programs, databases, trademarks, domain names, design solutions, works of science, literature, and art, the rights to which belong to the Company or third parties.
"Unlicensed Use" — use of the Services outside the scope of the granted license, including modification, decompilation, reverse engineering, distribution, reproduction, commercial use, etc.
"Technical Means" — equipment, devices, operating systems, browsers, and other technologies used by the User to interact with the Services.
"Force Majeure" — extraordinary and unavoidable circumstances preventing performance of obligations, including natural disasters, military actions, epidemics, communication network failures, power supply disruptions, and similar events.
3. TERMS OF USE
3.1. The Company grants the User the right to use the Services under a simple (non-exclusive), revocable, non-commercial, and non-transferable license, in accordance with Chapter 70 CC RB. The license is granted for the entire term of this Agreement unless otherwise provided by law or the Agreement itself.

3.2. The right to use the Services is granted exclusively for personal, non-commercial purposes. Any use of the Services for commercial, entrepreneurial, advertising, or other purposes is permitted only upon execution of a separate written agreement with the Company.

3.3. The User undertakes to use the Services in good faith, in accordance with their functional purpose, and in compliance with the legislation of the Republic of Belarus, including but not limited to:

the Law of the Republic of Belarus “On Information, Informatization, and Information Protection”;
the Law of the Republic of Belarus “On Personal Data Protection”;
the Law of the Republic of Belarus “On Advertising”;
the Law of the Republic of Belarus “On Citizens’ and Legal Entities’ Appeals to State Authorities”;
the Code of the Republic of Belarus on Administrative Offenses (CAO RB);
the Civil Code of the Republic of Belarus;
the Criminal Code of the Republic of Belarus.
3.4. Use of the Services is possible only after registration and/or authorization. During registration, the User undertakes to provide accurate information about themselves, including name, contact details, and other necessary identification data.

3.5. Creation of multiple accounts, fake profiles, or use of another person’s data without permission is prohibited and may result in liability under the legislation.

3.6. A User under the age of fourteen may use the Services only with the written consent of parents, adopters, or guardians, in accordance with Article 27 CC RB.

4. USER OBLIGATIONS
4.1. The User undertakes to:
a) Not carry out modification, decompilation, reverse engineering, reproduction, distribution, public display, import, export, commercial use, or any unauthorized use of intellectual property owned by the Company or third parties;
b) Not use automated data collection tools (scraping, bots, etc.), unauthorized server access, abuse of APIs, DDoS attacks, or any other methods violating security;
c) Not post, transmit, or publish Content that contains:

pornography, child erotica;
calls for violent constitutional changes, extremist activities;
defamation, insults, discriminatory statements;
information infringing on the rights of third parties, including copyright, related rights, trademarks, and others;
information that may harm the health, moral development, or psyche of minors;
knowingly false, misleading, or inaccurate information.
d) Not use the Services for spamming, phishing, fraud, cyberbullying, or other unlawful activities;
e) Not disclose account credentials to third parties or allow others to use the account without the Company's written consent;
f) Immediately notify the Administration of any unauthorized access to their account;
g) Comply with the rules of personal data processing established by the Law of the Republic of Belarus “On Personal Data Protection”, if the User acts as a personal data operator;
h) Not use the Services for purposes directly or indirectly causing damage to the interests of the state, society, third parties, or the Company;
i) Not block, modify, or disable advertisements included in the Services;
j) Not engage in actions aimed at gaining benefits not provided for in the usage conditions;
k) Not use the Services for unlawful purposes, including violations of the Constitution of the Republic of Belarus, criminal, administrative, or civil legislation;
l) Not violate confidentiality regimes applied to certain parts of the Services;
m) Follow digital ethics and respectful online behavior, respecting the rights and dignity of other Users;
n) Not perform actions affecting the performance, reliability, or availability of the Services;
o) Not use the Services bypassing technical restrictions imposed by the Company;
p) Not disclose information constituting commercial, service, technological, or other secrets of the Company obtained during the use of the Services.
5. LIABILITY
5.1. In case of breach of the Agreement terms, the Company has the right to:
a) Suspend, limit, or completely block the User’s access to the Services, including deletion of the account, without refund (if applicable);
b) Seek protection of violated rights in court in accordance with the law;
c) Claim compensation for damages, including actual damage, lost profits, court expenses, in accordance with Articles 933–944 CC RB;
d) Report the violation to law enforcement authorities if it involves signs of administrative or criminal offenses.

5.2. The Company’s liability is limited by Article 364 CC RB, according to which the maximum amount of damage compensation cannot exceed ten base units , as defined at the time of liability occurrence.

5.3. The Company shall not be liable for:
a) Accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of schedules, delays, or cancellations caused by force majeure, technical failures, or third-party actions, including carriers, providers, or government agencies;
b) Presence of errors, inaccuracies, or omissions in the information presented in the Services;
c) Interruptions in the operation of the Services caused by force majeure, communication network failures, power supply issues, or third-party actions;
d) Protection against viruses, malicious software, or unauthorized access unless due to the fault of the Company;
e) Content posted by the User or third parties, except when the Company has been officially notified of the violation and failed to take measures within a reasonable time frame.

5.4. The Company does not guarantee:
a) Full correspondence of the functionality to the declared characteristics;
b) Compatibility of the Services with all devices, operating systems, or browsers;
c) Absence of errors, malfunctions, or freezes in the Program.

6. DISPUTE RESOLUTION
6.1. All disputes arising from the conclusion, execution, amendment, or termination of the Agreement shall be resolved through negotiations between the parties.

6.2. If no agreement is reached, the dispute shall be submitted to the Arbitration Court of Gomel Region if it relates to entrepreneurial activity, or to the Gomel City Court if the dispute arises between a physical and a legal person.

6.3. Governing law — the legislation of the Republic of Belarus.

7. FINAL PROVISIONS
7.1. This Agreement comes into effect from the moment of its acceptance by the User and remains valid indefinitely unless terminated unilaterally by one of the parties.

7.2. The Company reserves the right to make changes to the Agreement unilaterally. Changes come into effect from the moment of publication in the “Legal Information” section of the application for Windows OS or on the official website unless otherwise provided by law.

7.3. Continued use of the Services after changes means acceptance of the new terms.

7.4. If any provision of the Agreement is recognized as invalid or legally ineffective, the remaining provisions remain in force.

7.5. All notices, requests, and inquiries related to the use of the Services should be sent to the email address specified in the “Contacts” section of the application or on the official website.

8. COMPANY DETAILS
Name: State Unitary Enterprise "Gomel Bus Park No. 1"
UNP: 123456789
Legal Address: Gomel, Sovetskaya St., 45
E-mail: support@blitzbus.by
Publication Date: June 24, 2025
Current Version: always available in the “Legal Information” section of the application for Windows OS.

⚠️ IMPORTANT! Use of the Services means that you have read, understood, and unconditionally accepted the terms of this Agreement. If you do not accept the terms, you must stop using the Services.
